            <ArticleTitle>Morphine equivalent normalized score (MENS) process for comparison of narcotic usage across colon surgery patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1092</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Current literature demonstrates how the use of narcotics prolongs a post-operative ileus [1]. An evidenced based care process model for a patient undergoing colon surgery requires the measurement of total narcotic usage. This includes all narcotics given during the patients stay. This care process model is being piloted at 5 different hospitals within Intermountain Health Care. A process was created analyzing narcotic usage within this population, which was named the morphine equivalent normalized score (MENS).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
